{"task_id": "Mbpp/12", "solution": "def sort_matrix(matrix: list[list[int]]) -> list[list[int]]:\n    \"\"\"Sorts the rows of a given matrix in ascending order according to the sum of its rows.\"\"\"\n\n    def _calculate_row_sum(row: list[int]) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Calculates the sum of all integer elements in a single row.\"\"\"\n        return sum(row)\n\n    # Create a list of (row_sum, original_row) tuples.\n    # We use a stable sort, so preserving original order for equal sums is not explicitly needed by the requirement,\n    # but using a list of tuples with the original row makes it straightforward.\n    rows_with_sums = []\n    for row in matrix:\n        rows_with_sums.append((_calculate_row_sum(row), row))\n\n    # Sort this list based on row_sum (the first element of the tuple).\n    rows_with_sums.sort(key=lambda x: x[0])\n\n    # Extract and return the original_rows in sorted order.\n    sorted_matrix = [row_tuple[1] for row_tuple in rows_with_sums]\n    return sorted_matrix"}
