{"task_id": "Mbpp/61", "solution": "def count_Substrings(s: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts substrings where the sum of digits equals the substring's length.\n    It iterates through all possible substrings and checks the condition.\n    \"\"\"\n    \n    # Helper function defined inline as required by instructions.\n    def _calculate_sum_of_digits(sub_str: str) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Calculates the sum of integer values of digits in a given substring.\"\"\"\n        current_sum = 0\n        for char_digit in sub_str:\n            current_sum += int(char_digit)\n        return current_sum\n\n    total_count = 0\n    n = len(s)\n\n    for i in range(n):\n        for j in range(i, n):\n            # Extract the current substring\n            substring = s[i : j + 1]\n            \n            # Calculate sum of digits and length using the inline helper\n            sum_of_digits = _calculate_sum_of_digits(substring)\n            substring_length = len(substring)\n            \n            # Check if the condition is met\n            if sum_of_digits == substring_length:\n                total_count += 1\n                \n    return total_count"}
