{"task_id": "Mbpp/109", "solution": "def odd_Equivalent(binary_string: str, rotation_count: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Finds the number of odd decimal equivalents when rotating a binary string.\n    Counts the total number of odd decimal numbers found across all rotations.\n    \"\"\"\n    def _rotate_string(s: str) -> str:\n        \"\"\"Rotates a string by moving its first character to the end.\"\"\"\n        if not s:\n            return \"\"\n        return s[1:] + s[0]\n\n    def _binary_to_decimal(binary_str: str) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Converts a binary string to its decimal integer equivalent.\"\"\"\n        return int(binary_str, 2)\n\n    def _is_odd(number: int) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Determines if an integer is odd.\"\"\"\n        return number % 2 != 0\n\n    odd_count = 0\n    current_binary_string = binary_string\n\n    for _ in range(rotation_count):\n        decimal_number = _binary_to_decimal(current_binary_string)\n        if _is_odd(decimal_number):\n            odd_count += 1\n        current_binary_string = _rotate_string(current_binary_string)\n\n    return odd_count"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/111", "solution": "def common_in_nested_lists(nested_list: list[list[Any]]) -> set[Any]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds common elements in given nested lists.\n    An element is considered common if it is present in every sub-list within the provided nested list.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not nested_list:\n        return set()\n\n    common_elements = set(nested_list[0])\n\n    for sub_list in nested_list[1:]:\n        if not common_elements:\n            return set()\n        common_elements.intersection_update(sub_list)\n\n    return common_elements"}
