{"task_id": "Mbpp/123", "solution": "def get_proper_divisors(n: int) -> list[int]:\n    \"\"\"Finds all proper divisors (excluding n itself) for a given positive integer.\"\"\"\n    if n <= 1:\n        return []\n    \n    divs = [1]\n    # Check divisors up to sqrt(n)\n    for i in range(2, int(n**0.5) + 1):\n        if n % i == 0:\n            divs.append(i)\n            if i * i != n:\n                divs.append(n // i)\n    return divs\ndef sum_proper_divisors(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the sum of all proper divisors for a given positive integer.\"\"\"\n    return sum(get_proper_divisors(n))\ndef _is_amicable_pair(a: int, b: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Determines if two distinct positive integers form an amicable pair.\"\"\"\n    if a == b:\n        return False\n    return sum_proper_divisors(a) == b and sum_proper_divisors(b) == a\ndef amicable_numbers_sum(upper_limit: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the sum of all amicable numbers from 1 up to a specified upper limit.\"\"\"\n    amicable_numbers_set = set()\n\n    for n in range(1, upper_limit + 1):\n        if n in amicable_numbers_set:\n            continue\n\n        # d_n is the sum of proper divisors for n\n        d_n = sum_proper_divisors(n)\n\n        # Check for potential amicable pair (n, d_n)\n        # Ensure d_n is within limits and n is less than d_n to avoid redundant checks and self-amicable numbers.\n        if n < d_n and d_n <= upper_limit:\n            if _is_amicable_pair(n, d_n):\n                amicable_numbers_set.add(n)\n                amicable_numbers_set.add(d_n)\n\n    return sum(amicable_numbers_set)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/125", "solution": "def find_length(binary_string: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the maximum difference between the count of '0's and '1's in any contiguous substring.\n    Uses Kadane's algorithm adaptation where '0's contribute +1 and '1's contribute -1.\n    \"\"\"\n    max_so_far = 0\n    current_max = 0\n\n    for char in binary_string:\n        # Transforms '0' to +1 and '1' to -1, inlining the _transform_char logic.\n        transformed_value = 1 if char == '0' else -1\n\n        current_max += transformed_value\n\n        # If current_max becomes negative, reset it to 0, as a new substring could start.\n        if current_max < 0:\n            current_max = 0\n\n        # Update the overall maximum difference found so far.\n        max_so_far = max(max_so_far, current_max)\n\n    return max_so_far"}
