{"task_id": "Mbpp/141", "solution": "def pancake_sort(input_list):\n    \"\"\"Sorts a list of comparable elements in ascending order using the Pancake Sort algorithm.\"\"\"\n    arr = list(input_list) # Create a copy to avoid modifying the original list\n    n = len(arr)\n\n    # This helper function reverses the sub-array arr[0...k] in-place.\n    def _flip(arr_to_flip, k):\n        start = 0\n        while start < k:\n            arr_to_flip[start], arr_to_flip[k] = arr_to_flip[k], arr_to_flip[start]\n            start += 1\n            k -= 1\n\n    # This helper function finds the index of the maximum element in arr[0...n-1].\n    def _find_max_index(arr_to_search, n_elements):\n        max_val = arr_to_search[0]\n        max_idx = 0\n        for i in range(1, n_elements):\n            if arr_to_search[i] > max_val:\n                max_val = arr_to_search[i]\n                max_idx = i\n        return max_idx\n\n    for curr_size in range(n, 1, -1):\n        # Find the index of the maximum element in the current unsorted prefix (arr[0...curr_size-1])\n        max_idx = _find_max_index(arr, curr_size)\n\n        # If the maximum element is not already at the end of the current prefix\n        if max_idx != curr_size - 1:\n            # Flip the sub-array from 0 to max_idx to bring the maximum element to the front\n            _flip(arr, max_idx)\n            # Flip the sub-array from 0 to curr_size-1 to move the maximum element to its correct sorted position\n            _flip(arr, curr_size - 1)\n            \n    return arr"}
