{"task_id": "Mbpp/227", "solution": "def min_of_three(number1: float, number2: float, number3: float) -> float:\n    \"\"\"Finds the minimum of three numerical inputs.\n\n    Args:\n        number1 (float): The first numerical input.\n        number2 (float): The second numerical input.\n        number3 (float): The third numerical input.\n\n    Returns:\n        float: The smallest value among the three inputs.\n\n    Raises:\n        TypeError: If any of the inputs are not numerical.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not all(isinstance(arg, (int, float)) for arg in [number1, number2, number3]):\n        raise TypeError(\"All inputs must be numerical (int or float).\")\n\n    minimum_value = number1\n    if number2 < minimum_value:\n        minimum_value = number2\n    if number3 < minimum_value:\n        minimum_value = number3\n    return minimum_value"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/224", "solution": "def count_Set_Bits(number: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts the number of set bits (binary digits with value 1) in a given integer.\n    Uses Brian Kernighan's algorithm for efficient counting.\n    \"\"\"\n    count = 0\n    while number > 0:\n        number &= (number - 1)\n        count += 1\n    return count"}
