{"task_id": "Mbpp/223", "solution": "def _find_first_occurrence(arr: list[int], target: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Finds the index of the first occurrence of a target element in a sorted array using binary search.\n    Returns the length of the array if the target is not found.\"\"\"\n    low = 0\n    high = len(arr) - 1\n    result = len(arr)\n\n    while low <= high:\n        mid = low + (high - low) // 2\n        if arr[mid] == target:\n            result = mid\n            high = mid - 1\n        elif arr[mid] < target:\n            low = mid + 1\n        else: # arr[mid] > target\n            high = mid - 1\n    return result\ndef _find_last_occurrence(arr: list[int], target: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Finds the index of the last occurrence of a target element in a sorted array using binary search.\n    Returns -1 if the target is not found.\"\"\"\n    low = 0\n    high = len(arr) - 1\n    result = -1\n\n    while low <= high:\n        mid = low + (high - low) // 2\n        if arr[mid] == target:\n            result = mid\n            low = mid + 1\n        elif arr[mid] < target:\n            low = mid + 1\n        else: # arr[mid] > target\n            high = mid - 1\n    return result\ndef is_majority(sorted_array: list[int], n: int, element: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Checks if an element is the majority element in a sorted array.\n    A majority element occurs more than n/2 times.\"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return False\n\n    first_idx = _find_first_occurrence(sorted_array, element)\n\n    # If the element is not found, first_idx will be n\n    if first_idx == n:\n        return False\n\n    last_idx = _find_last_occurrence(sorted_array, element)\n\n    count = last_idx - first_idx + 1\n    majority_threshold = n / 2.0\n\n    return count > majority_threshold"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/232", "solution": "def larg_nnum(input_list: list, n: int) -> list:\n    \"\"\"\n    Returns a list containing the n largest items from the input list.\n    Handles edge cases for n and empty lists as per design rules.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n <= 0 or not input_list:\n        return []\n\n    sorted_list = sorted(input_list, reverse=True)\n\n    if n >= len(sorted_list):\n        return sorted_list\n    else:\n        return sorted_list[:n]"}
