{"task_id": "Mbpp/260", "solution": "def newman_prime(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the nth Newman-Shanks-Williams prime number.\n    Raises ValueError if n is negative.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    if n < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"n must be a non-negative integer.\")\n\n    # Calculate S_n using the recurrence relation\n    s_values = [1, 1]  # S_0 = 1, S_1 = 1\n    if n < len(s_values):\n        s_n = s_values[n]\n    else:\n        for i in range(2, n + 1):\n            s_i = 2 * s_values[i - 1] + s_values[i - 2]\n            s_values.append(s_i)\n        s_n = s_values[n]\n\n    # Check for primality of S_n\n    if s_n < 2:\n        return None # 0 and 1 are not prime\n    for i in range(2, int(s_n**0.5) + 1):\n        if s_n % i == 0:\n            return None # s_n is not prime\n    \n    return s_n"}
