{"task_id": "Mbpp/283", "solution": "def validate(integer_value: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if the frequency of each digit in an integer is less than or equal to the digit itself.\n    This function orchestrates digit extraction, frequency calculation, and condition checking.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def _extract_digits(integer_value: int) -> list[int]:\n        \"\"\"Converts an integer into a list of its constituent digits, handling its absolute value.\"\"\"\n        if integer_value == 0:\n            return [0]\n        digits = []\n        # Convert to string to handle negative numbers and extract digits easily\n        s_value = str(abs(integer_value))\n        for char_digit in s_value:\n            digits.append(int(char_digit))\n        return digits\n\n    def _calculate_frequencies(digits: list[int]) -> dict[int, int]:\n        \"\"\"Computes the frequency (count of occurrences) of each unique digit.\"\"\"\n        frequencies = {}\n        for digit in digits:\n            frequencies[digit] = frequencies.get(digit, 0) + 1\n        return frequencies\n\n    def _check_frequency_condition(frequencies: dict[int, int]) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Verifies if each digit's frequency is less than or equal to its numerical value.\"\"\"\n        for digit, frequency in frequencies.items():\n            if frequency > digit:\n                return False\n        return True\n\n    digits_list = _extract_digits(integer_value)\n    frequencies_map = _calculate_frequencies(digits_list)\n    validation_result = _check_frequency_condition(frequencies_map)\n    return validation_result"}
