{"task_id": "Mbpp/398", "solution": "def sum_of_digits(numbers: list[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Computes the total sum of digits for a given list of non-negative integers.\n    It orchestrates the process by iterating through the list and calling a helper function for individual number processing.\n    \"\"\"\n    def _sum_digits_of_single_number(number: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"\n        Calculates the sum of individual digits for a single non-negative integer.\n        This is an internal helper function.\n        \"\"\"\n        digit_sum = 0\n        while number > 0:\n            digit_sum += number % 10\n            number //= 10\n        return digit_sum\n\n    total_aggregated_sum = 0\n    for num in numbers:\n        total_aggregated_sum += _sum_digits_of_single_number(num)\n    return total_aggregated_sum"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/392", "solution": "_memo = {0: 0}\ndef get_max_sum(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the maximum sum for a given non-negative integer n using memoization.\n    The function applies the recursive formula f(n) = max( (f(n/2) + f(n/3) + f(n/4) + f(n/5)), n).\n    \"\"\"\n    if n in _memo:\n        return _memo[n]\n\n    sum_of_parts = (get_max_sum(n // 2) +\n                    get_max_sum(n // 3) +\n                    get_max_sum(n // 4) +\n                    get_max_sum(n // 5))\n\n    current_max_sum = max(sum_of_parts, n)\n    _memo[n] = current_max_sum\n    return current_max_sum"}
