{"task_id": "Mbpp/419", "solution": "def round_and_sum(numbers: list[float]) -> float:\n    \"\"\"\n    Rounds every number in a list, sums them, and multiplies the sum by the list's length.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    class Number:\n        \"\"\"Encapsulates a single numerical value and provides rounding functionality.\"\"\"\n        def __init__(self, value: float):\n            self._value = value\n\n        def get_value(self) -> float:\n            return self._value\n\n        def round(self) -> int:\n            return round(self._value)\n\n    class ListOfNumbers:\n        \"\"\"Manages a collection of Number objects, calculates sum of rounded numbers and list length.\"\"\"\n        def __init__(self, numbers_list: list[float]):\n            self._numbers: list[Number] = []\n            for num_float in numbers_list:\n                self._numbers.append(Number(num_float))\n\n        def add_number(self, number_float: float):\n            self._numbers.append(Number(number_float))\n\n        def get_length(self) -> int:\n            return len(self._numbers)\n\n        def get_rounded_sum(self) -> float:\n            total_rounded_sum = 0\n            for num_obj in self._numbers:\n                total_rounded_sum += num_obj.round()\n            return float(total_rounded_sum)\n\n    class Result:\n        \"\"\"Stores and provides access to the final calculated value.\"\"\"\n        def __init__(self, final_value: float):\n            self._final_value = final_value\n\n        def get_final_value(self) -> float:\n            return self._final_value\n\n    list_of_numbers_instance = ListOfNumbers(numbers)\n    \n    list_length = list_of_numbers_instance.get_length()\n    sum_of_rounded_numbers = list_of_numbers_instance.get_rounded_sum()\n    \n    final_calculated_value = sum_of_rounded_numbers * list_length\n    \n    result_instance = Result(final_calculated_value)\n    \n    return result_instance.get_final_value()"}
