{"task_id": "Mbpp/445", "solution": "def index_multiplication(tuple1: tuple, tuple2: tuple) -> tuple:\n    \"\"\"\n    Performs index-wise multiplication of elements in two tuples.\n    It handles nested tuples and multiplies corresponding numerical elements.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(tuple1, tuple) or not isinstance(tuple2, tuple):\n        raise ValueError(\"Both inputs must be tuples.\")\n\n    if len(tuple1) != len(tuple2):\n        raise ValueError(\"Tuples must have identical dimensions at each level.\")\n\n    result_elements = []\n    for i in range(len(tuple1)):\n        elem1, elem2 = tuple1[i], tuple2[i]\n\n        if isinstance(elem1, tuple) and isinstance(elem2, tuple):\n            result_elements.append(index_multiplication(elem1, elem2))\n        elif isinstance(elem1, (int, float)) and isinstance(elem2, (int, float)):\n            result_elements.append(elem1 * elem2)\n        else:\n            # This case covers type mismatches (e.g., number vs tuple)\n            # or unsupported types if the problem statement implies only numbers/tuples.\n            raise ValueError(f\"Mismatched element types or unsupported types at index {i}: {type(elem1)} vs {type(elem2)}\")\n\n    return tuple(result_elements)"}
