{"task_id": "Mbpp/583", "solution": "def catalan_number(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the nth Catalan number using dynamic programming.\n    Raises ValueError if n is negative.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input 'n' must be a non-negative integer.\")\n    if n == 0:\n        return 1\n\n    catalan = [0] * (n + 1)\n    catalan[0] = 1\n\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        for j in range(i):\n            catalan[i] += catalan[j] * catalan[i - 1 - j]\n\n    return catalan[n]"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/585", "solution": "def expensive_items(dataset: list[dict], n: int) -> list[dict]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the n most expensive items in a given dataset.\n    Items are sorted by price in descending order.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"n must be a non-negative integer.\")\n\n    # Sort the dataset by 'price' in descending order\n    sorted_items = sorted(dataset, key=lambda item: item['price'], reverse=True)\n\n    # Return the top 'n' items. If fewer than 'n' items exist, return all.\n    return sorted_items[:n]"}
