{"task_id": "Mbpp/622", "solution": "def get_median(list1: list[float], list2: list[float], n: int) -> float:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the median of two sorted lists of the same size.\n    Assumes list1 and list2 are sorted and have size n.\n    \"\"\"\n    i = 0  # Pointer for list1\n    j = 0  # Pointer for list2\n    \n    prev_element = 0.0  # Stores the (k-1)-th smallest element from the merged lists\n    current_element = 0.0 # Stores the k-th smallest element from the merged lists\n\n    # Iterate n+1 times to find the elements at index n-1 and n (0-indexed)\n    # The median for 2n elements is the average of elements at index n-1 and n.\n    for _ in range(n + 1):\n        prev_element = current_element\n\n        if i < n and j < n:\n            if list1[i] < list2[j]:\n                current_element = list1[i]\n                i += 1\n            else:\n                current_element = list2[j]\n                j += 1\n        elif i < n:  # list2 is exhausted, take from list1\n            current_element = list1[i]\n            i += 1\n        else:  # list1 is exhausted, take from list2 (j must be < n)\n            current_element = list2[j]\n            j += 1\n            \n    return (prev_element + current_element) / 2.0"}
