{"task_id": "Mbpp/743", "solution": "def rotate_right(input_list: list, rotation_count: int) -> list:\n    \"\"\"\n    Rotates a list to the right by the specified number of positions, returning a new list.\n    Handles negative rotation counts, empty lists, and rotations exceeding list length.\n    \"\"\"\n    if rotation_count < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"rotation_count must be a non-negative integer.\")\n\n    if not input_list:\n        return []\n\n    list_length = len(input_list)\n    effective_rotation = rotation_count % list_length\n\n    if effective_rotation == 0:\n        return list(input_list) # Return a copy to adhere to \"return new list\" BR4\n\n    rotated_list = input_list[-effective_rotation:] + input_list[:-effective_rotation]\n    return rotated_list"}
