{"task_id": "Mbpp/745", "solution": "def divisible_by_digits(startnum: int, endnum: int) -> list[int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds numbers within a given range where every number is divisible by every digit it contains.\n    Helper functions are used for digit extraction and divisibility checks.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def _get_digits(number: int) -> list[int]:\n        \"\"\"Extracts individual digits from a given integer.\"\"\"\n        if number == 0:\n            return [0]\n        digits = []\n        temp_num = abs(number)\n        while temp_num > 0:\n            digits.append(temp_num % 10)\n            temp_num //= 10\n        return digits[::-1]\n\n    def _is_divisible_by_digit(number: int, digit: int) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Checks if a number is perfectly divisible by a given non-zero digit.\"\"\"\n        if digit == 0:\n            return False\n        return number % digit == 0\n\n    def _is_valid_number(number: int) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Determines if a number is divisible by all its non-zero digits.\"\"\"\n        digits = _get_digits(number)\n        for digit in digits:\n            if digit == 0:\n                continue  # Ignore zero digits for divisibility check\n            if not _is_divisible_by_digit(number, digit):\n                return False\n        return True\n\n    collected_numbers = []\n    for number in range(startnum, endnum + 1):\n        if _is_valid_number(number):\n            collected_numbers.append(number)\n    return collected_numbers"}
