{"task_id": "Mbpp/793", "solution": "def last(array: list, element: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the last position (highest index) of an element in a sorted array.\n    Uses a modified binary search to efficiently locate the last occurrence.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(array)\n    if n == 0:\n        return -1\n\n    low = 0\n    high = n - 1\n    result = -1\n\n    while low <= high:\n        mid = low + (high - low) // 2\n        if array[mid] == element:\n            result = mid\n            low = mid + 1\n        elif array[mid] < element:\n            low = mid + 1\n        else:  # array[mid] > element\n            high = mid - 1\n    return result"}
