{"task_id": "Mbpp/799", "solution": "def left_rotate(n: int, d: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Rotates the bits of a 32-bit integer 'n' to the left by 'd' positions.\n    Python integers handle arbitrary precision, so explicit masking is needed to simulate 32-bit behavior.\n    \"\"\"\n    d = d % 32\n    return ((n << d) | (n >> (32 - d))) & 0xFFFFFFFF"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/803", "solution": "def is_perfect_square(number: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if the given non-negative integer is a perfect square.\n    It calculates the integer square root and compares its square to the original number.\n    \"\"\"\n    if number < 0:\n        return False\n    \n    # Calculate the integer square root\n    sqrt_num = int(number**0.5)\n    \n    # Check if the square of the integer square root equals the original number\n    return sqrt_num * sqrt_num == number"}
