{"task_id": "Mbpp/806", "solution": "def max_run_uppercase(input_string: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the maximum run of consecutive uppercase characters in the given string.\n    Returns the length of the longest run, or 0 if no uppercase characters are found.\n    \"\"\"\n    max_run = 0\n    current_run = 0\n    for char in input_string:\n        if char.isupper():\n            current_run += 1\n            max_run = max(max_run, current_run)\n        else:\n            current_run = 0\n    return max_run"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/805", "solution": "def max_sum_list(list_of_lists: list[list[int]]) -> list[int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Returns the inner list from a list of lists whose sum of elements is the highest.\n\n    Args:\n        list_of_lists: A list of lists, where each inner list contains numeric elements.\n\n    Returns:\n        The inner list with the highest sum. If the input list_of_lists is empty,\n        an empty list is returned.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not list_of_lists:\n        return []\n\n    return max(list_of_lists, key=sum)"}
